is eric killmonger back in the black  panther sequel or have we gotten our  first shot of shuri as the new warrior  queen based on one shot from the wakanda  forever trailer fans think they've  already gotten it all figured out he has  everything you need to know bury me in  the ocean  with my ancestors that jump from the  ships  because they knew death  was better than bondage  these were the final words eric  killmonger uttered in black panther  after the death of t'challa actor  chadwick boseman though the concept of  death in the advanced city of wakanda is  now seen in an all-new light fans are  eagerly anticipating the sequel to the  massively successful first outing but  the franchise's direction has been an  open question without the lead actor  sumab even hopes that mike will be  jordan's killmonger would be resurrected  redeemed and given the mantle of  wakanda's legendary protector who the  next black panther will be remains a  mystery but thankfully marvel and  director ryan coogler have found their  direction as seen in the first trailer  for black panther wakanda forever the  nation will be going to war with  atlantis and the fearsome leader neymar  the submariner it seems clear that the  next person to done the mask of the  panther won't be fully revealed until  it's much closer to the time for the  movie to hit theaters allowing fan  theories to develop in the months  leading up to it  there are a number of worthy successes  to the mantle t'challa's sister shuri  becomes black panther in the comics so  there are certainly canonical reasons  for her to assume the legacy there's  also nakia who played a pivotal role in  the first film and managed to convince  t'challa to bring wakanda's  contributions to the light however fans  have a different idea entirely as to who  will be the next black panther it all  comes down to one tease at the end of  the trailer that has a number of fans  speculating a wild twist  throughout the trailer fans are treated  to scene after scene of colourful  costumes impressive landscapes and a  stellar soundtrack we get a glimpse of  neymar and the forces of atlantis as  well as the wakanda clearly reeling over  the death of their king and even a  highly anticipated look at the first  appearance of riri williams aka iron  heart what we don't get is a lot of  insight on the mantle of the black  panther or who will be wearing the suit  until the end of the trailer where the  newest protector of wakanda is seen from  behind on a beach ready for battle the  most telling part of the scene perhaps  is not that we see who is in the suit  but the suit itself as one of the small  details noted by fans online is that  this newest look has a gold trim and  stylings of killmonger suit in contrast  to the shades previously worn by  t'challa which were more purple there's  also currently a lot of back and forth  on twitter about whether the person in  the suit has a masculine frame or a  feminine one in response to the scene in  the trailer one fan just said simply  please be michael b jordan others agreed  with another fan proposing the notion  that if killmonger's final wish were  honored perhaps neymar found his body in  the ocean and revived him not everyone  agrees of course with many believing  that the suited figure is shuri  including one who writes  shuri is a new black panther and she  will slay still a fair number of fans  believe or wish it to be the triumphant  return of michael b jordan as eric  killmonger we'll just have to see for  ourselves what's in store when black  panther wakanda forever hits theaters on  november 11th  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies and tv shows are  coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]
 

